{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01RHvAnLYQqY2VtxKWAW9Uop","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a direct read of the member document `anchor_gui.py` (8,093 lines), here is the grounded session summary:\n\n## Summary â€” `anchor_gui.py`\n\n**What it is**\n- `anchor_gui.py` is the self-contained Anchor application: a Python-stdlib HTTP server that generates the full dashboard HTML per request and writes directly to the markdown files. *(grounded: module structure; `generate_html` at L4320, `class AnchorHandler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler)` at L6270)*\n\n**Server / runtime**\n- It binds loopback by default via `make_server(host=\"127.0.0.1\", port=8777)` (L7970) and uses an `_ExclusiveThreadingHTTPServer` (L7941) â€” the single-instance guard so a duplicate process can't squat on port 8777.\n- `resolve_bind_host()` (L7999) and `main()` (L8019) own startup; a `_heartbeat_watchdog()` (L7930) runs alongside.\n- A computed build id (`_compute_build_id` L78) plus `cache_bust_script()` (L144) drive cache-busting.\n\n**Markdown task engine (the original Anchor core)**\n- Parsing helpers read markdown into dicts: `parse_tasks_from_md` (L181), `parse_projects_from_md` (L243), `parse_inbox_from_md` (L285), `parse_archived_tasks` (L298); `gather_all()` (L319) aggregates DASHBOARD + domain files.\n- Change operations are write-locked via `_with_write_lock` (L3885): `mark_done`/`mark_undone` (L3908/3932), `add_task` (L3956), `capture_inbox` (L3984), `edit_task` (L4043), `edit_project` (L4133), `cancel_task` (L4266), `save_for_later` (L4277), `restore_task` (L4288), `log_change` (L3894).\n\n**R&D control surface (v2â†’v4) embedded in the GUI**\n- Project window: `render_project_window_html` (L1856, ~1,800 lines) plus tile/kanban renderers â€” `render_project_tile_html` (L1106), `_render_kanban_html` (L1618), `_render_lane_sessions` (L1693), `_render_grass_board` (L1579), `render_deliverables_html` (L3785).\n- Sum